cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the EVEWorld paper."
title: "EVEWorld: Physical Evolution Supervision for Embodied World Models"
abstract: >-
  EVEWorld supervises target-instance evolution in embodied video world
  models to overcome Model Laziness: Instance-Guided Restoration (IGR)
  restores clean videos from duplicate-corrupted inputs, Temporal Instance
  Alignment (TIA) promotes local cross-frame target correspondence, and the
  Model Laziness Rate (MLR) measures persistent target-count violations.
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous Author(s)"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
url: "https://behappya.github.io/EVEWorld/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/behappya/EVEWorld"
keywords:
  - world models
  - video generation
  - embodied AI
  - robot manipulation
  - physical evolution
